# Playing the first release, from orbit to a second territory.
#
# `releases/first-release.md` gives the loop in eight steps. This file walks the first
# five: no presence on the planet, land the ark and found a territory, work the food
# extractor to grow the population, build extractors for metal and energy, then produce a
# pioneer and spread across the planet by land.
#
# Every line is a command. There is no other way for the state to move, so this file is a
# complete account of the game it produces.

# 1 and 2. The ark comes down, and landing *is* the founding: it takes the ground and
# becomes a garrison to hold it, a citizen, and an extractor on the best food node. One
# action, so the farm can be worked the same turn.
land ark 1

# 3. Work the food extractor to grow the population.
work 1 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 2. Two citizens: one opens a second food node, one works the first.
build extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 3. Four citizens. The third food node is taken and every farm is worked.
build extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 4. Eight citizens. Food first, then step 4: extractors on the metal nodes.
work 3 extractor 1 food
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 metal
work 2 extractor 1 metal
end turn

# Turn 5. Twelve citizens, which is every hand the food here can feed, and twelve units of
# labor. All three resources are worked to the territory's ceiling: twelve of each.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 energy
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# 5. Twelve metal and twelve energy are on the ground and a pioneer costs eight and six,
# so the landing site can send one out.
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 6. The farms are worked first - a population that gathers nothing this turn starves
# at the end of it, whatever else is going on.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# The pioneer crosses into a neighbouring territory. It is not held, so arriving there
# takes it and founds it: force 2 against a force of nature of 1, and the pioneer becomes
# the garrison, citizen and food extractor the new ground needs.
move pioneer 2

# The new territory arrives with a citizen and a farm, both ready, so it can feed itself
# on the very turn it is founded. A citizen that gathers nothing starves at the end of the
# turn like any other, so founding late in a turn and leaving the farm idle costs the
# citizen the founding just produced.
work 1 extractor 2 food
end turn
